# The RGD parser's normalizer, checked against a truth table.
#
# driver/normtest.cpp synthesizes a union table for a random boolean formula
# over independent relational leaves, runs it through
# find_roots -> to_nnf -> to_dnf -> construct_task, reads the DNF back out of
# the tasks, and compares the two over every assignment.  Nothing here needs a
# compiler or an instrumented target -- the label store is built in memory --
# so the whole file runs in well under a second.
#
# Four configurations rather than one long run, because they stress different
# parts of the pipeline and a single shape would leave the others at zero:
#
#   deep + few leaves     the xor expansion, which doubles the tree, and the
#                         arena bound that stops it (see arena_full=)
#   shallow + many leaves wide DNFs and a bigger truth table per formula
#   high --boolcmp-pct    the `bool ==/!= 0/1` arm of find_roots' icmp case,
#                         which is a connective (copy or LNot), not a fold
#   --const-pct           an rgd::Bool below the root, which every arm of
#                         find_roots has to fold rather than wrap (#130)
#
# The --const-pct runs need the last one spelled out, because the shape they
# generate -- a constant operand to a boolean connective -- is one
# __taint_union() folds away before a label exists, so it cannot arrive from a
# trace.  The Bool node it produces can: find_roots concretizes an ICmp leaf
# whose operand subtrees exceed max_ast_size into exactly that.  This is the
# only way we generate it, and it caught a real bug -- the bool-icmp arm wrapped
# such a child in LNot instead of folding it, which to_nnf then refused
# ("unexpected node kind") or construct_task quietly dropped, the latter
# producing tasks weaker than the clause they came from.  Before the fix these
# three runs reported unsound=3/8/9, lossy=2/4/5 and incomplete=36/92/182.  See
# gen_term() in the driver.
#
# unsound= and lossy= are asserted separately because only one of the two can
# mislead a solver.  unsound means the DNF admits an assignment that does not
# reach the target direction, so a solution to it need not flip the branch;
# lossy means solutions were dropped.  Both fail the run -- the parser owes
# exact equivalence -- but a regression in the first is a wrong answer and one
# in the second is lost coverage, and one counter cannot say which.
#
# The last three runs add --strict, which is construct_task's other policy for
# a conjunct that will not parse: drop the whole clause rather than hand out
# the weakened one.  Lenient is what the fuzzer runs -- a candidate input that
# does not flip the branch costs one execution and may still find coverage, so
# trying beats not trying -- and strict is for a consumer that has to trust a
# task.  Both are run because the same defect surfaces differently under them,
# which is also how the two halves of the #130 fix were shown to be
# independent: with the leak restored, these configurations report unsound=9/7/8
# under lenient and unsound=0 lossy=5/7/6 under --strict.  Either way the run
# fails; the counter that moves says which policy was in force.
#
# checked= is asserted non-zero on purpose: every other outcome (folded,
# arena_full) is a legitimate refusal that the driver counts rather than fails,
# so a regression that refused *everything* would otherwise report PASS.
#
# RUN: %normtest --seed 1 --cases 5000 --depth 3 --leaves 4 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 2 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --leaves 3 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 3 --cases 2000 --depth 6 --leaves 6 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 4 --cases 5000 --depth 2 --leaves 8 --boolcmp-pct 40 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 5 --cases 5000 --depth 4 --leaves 5 --boolcmp-pct 60 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 1 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 10 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 1 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 25 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 1 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 50 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 1 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 50 --strict 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 2 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 50 --strict 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %normtest --seed 3 --cases 5000 --depth 5 --const-pct 50 --strict 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
#
# CHECK: NORM-SUMMARY cases={{[0-9]+}} checked={{[1-9][0-9]*}}
# CHECK-SAME: unsound=0 lossy=0 incomplete=0 harness=0
# CHECK: NORM-RESULT PASS
